{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\n\nRemove the legacy `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check` CLI/direct-engine command and its `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` status artifact without breaking the canonical bridge surfaces that replaced its observables. Retain the engine-only legacy-route `--filter-local-ids` post-filter because the active live Jira DC CI harness needs verbatim raw-key scoping for not-yet-bound inbound creates that primary `--only` cannot express.\n\nReplacement is distributed:\n- `rebar bridge preview` is the live Jira-vs-local differ/proposed-change observable.\n- `rebar bridge fsck --output json` is the offline orphan/unbound/binding-drift audit observable.\n- `rebar bridge status --json` remains the status surface, but no longer reads stale `reconcile-check.json`.\n\nPreserve `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"`: it is read back at runtime via `Mode.from_str` in `_advisory_lock._mode_blocks`, so `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` MUST stay in the enum/`_ORDERED` or a paused repo silently stops blocking. Remove only the CLI command, not the internal mode.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `_bridge_runner.py`: repoint retained `reconcile-check` profile to `rebar bridge preview`, not fsck.\n- `_cli/_registry.py`, `_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py`, `_cli/help/reconcile.txt`: remove top-level `rebar reconcile` and `--mode reconcile-check` CLI surface. Keep `--filter-local-ids` on the direct-engine legacy route only; reject it on primary `preview`/`sync`.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`: delete `_run_reconcile_check`, its JSON writer, and its `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` dispatch branch; keep the legacy-route `filter_local_ids` handoff into `run_pass`.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`: remove legacy-route `--mode reconcile-check` parsing while retaining `--filter-local-ids` on the direct-engine legacy route; keep canonical `preview`/`sync` and reject the post-filter flag there.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py`: RETAIN `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` + its `_ORDERED`/`MODE_CAPS` entries (load-bearing for the advisory-lock pause gate via `Mode.from_str(\"reconcile-check\")`); only revise the docstring wording that describes it as the removed CLI command.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py`: remove reconcile-check no-write logic/wording.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py`: remove `_read_reconcile_diagnostics()` and `snapshot()[\"reconcile_diagnostics\"]`.\n- `_mcp_models.py`, `schemas/bridge_status.schema.json`, `types.py`: remove `reconcile_diagnostics` from BridgeStatus model/schema/types so MCP no longer advertises a producerless field.\n- `_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py`: delete orphaned legacy report module.\n- Update stale reconcile-check wording in `binding_recovery.py`, `binding_walk.py`, `fetcher.py`, `get_rotation.py`, `load_phase.py`, `pass_support.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, and `ticket_planner.py`.\n- Update workflow/probe/docs/changelog references that instruct `reconcile-check`, using preview for live discrepancy checks and fsck for offline orphan/unbound audits.\n- Tests (enum retained, so all `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` references stay valid — only removed-symbol consumers change): DELETE the `reconcile_check.py`-module tests `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_check{,_canonical,_canonical_heldout,_bindings_dict}.py` (they exercise the removed `_run_reconcile_check`/`reconcile_check.reconcile_check()`); migrate `test_reconcile_filter.py` to keep engine-only `--filter-local-ids` legacy-route parsing/handoff while rejecting it on primary bridge verbs. Grep the reconciler test tree for the removed symbols and fix any remaining consumer (leave enum/sentinel references intact). Add BridgeStatus model/schema-parity + preview-probe coverage. `make test` is an AC.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n1. `bridge fsck` is not the sole replacement: it is offline and exits 1 on findings, whereas legacy reconcile-check exited 0.\n2. `_bridge_runner.MODE_COMMANDS[\"reconcile-check\"]` maps to `rebar bridge preview`, whose canonical route emits JSON on stdout and `BRIDGE_STATE: <state>` on stderr with 0/1/2 exit semantics.\n3. After `_run_reconcile_check` is deleted, no canonical writer refreshes `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`; remove all status/model/schema readers instead of creating a new writer.\n4. Remove `BridgeStatusOut.reconcile_diagnostics` in `_mcp_models.py`; schema drift will not catch an extra permissive model field, so add explicit MCP/schema parity coverage.\n5. Pressure probes must stop grepping legacy prose (`0 discrepancies`, `discrepancy`, `mismatch`). Run canonical `preview --only ... --repo-root ...`, preserve the exit code, parse the final stdout JSON, and pass only when `route==\"preview\"`, `mutation_count==0`, and `plan` contains no entry for the probe key/local id.\n6. Keep `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel `reconcile-check` byte-for-byte, AND keep `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` in the enum/`_ORDERED`/`MODE_CAPS`: the sentinel is decoded back through `Mode.from_str` by `_advisory_lock._mode_blocks`, so removing the enum would make `from_str(\"reconcile-check\")` raise and the pause gate fail open.\n7. Retain `--filter-local-ids` on the direct-engine legacy route because live-DC-in-GHA uses its post-filter semantics for inbound creates where the raw Jira key has no binding yet; follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0` still owns deeper selection/filter plumbing cleanup.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py` proves `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` + its `_ORDERED`/`MODE_CAPS` entries are RETAINED and `Mode.from_str(\"reconcile-check\")` still round-trips (pause gate intact); ordering works.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` proves `--mode reconcile-check` rejects and `_run_reconcile_check` is not dispatched.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py` proves the retained runner profile invokes `bridge preview`, not fsck, and preserves delivery semantics.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py` proves orphaned bindings/Jira and unbound local/Jira remain in `bridge fsck --output json`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py` proves BridgeStatus library/MCP/schema/types no longer expose `reconcile_diagnostics`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_jira_pressure_probe_preview_assertions_heldout.py` proves both pressure probes migrated from legacy prose greps to preview JSON assertions on `route`, `mutation_count`, and absence of probe targets in `plan`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py` proves pause documents still preserve `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py` proves the top-level `rebar reconcile` route and direct `--mode reconcile-check` remain rejected, the engine-only `--filter-local-ids` legacy-route post-filter parses/hands off raw Jira keys for inbound creates, and primary `preview`/`sync` still reject the flag.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test` passes.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out oracles: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb_heldout.py` (CLI-removal, BridgeStatus diagnostics removal, and pause-sentinel regression), `tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py` (engine-only `--filter-local-ids` restoration and primary-verb rejection), and `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py` plus the pressure-probe script tests for the reconciler-core/probe migration. All proving commands are enumerated under Acceptance Criteria.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Do not edit `_lib_ops.py` or `_mcp_reads.py`; c195 already removed Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)`.\n- Do not remove the engine-only `--filter-local-ids` legacy-route post-filter; `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0` owns any later redesign of selection/filter plumbing.\n- Do not change `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel bytes/schema.\n- Do not change canonical preview/sync/fsck/status semantics except removing stale status diagnostics.\n- Do not force any ticket operation; rerun plan-review and completion verification through the normal gates."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788552257817605322,"uuid":"2756854e-6d4f-47c9-ad97-3cf2a18a4835"}